 " is the search."
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"40e899d3-f917-49ab-8f42-8f5174773a30"],

Cell["\<\
Definition: a line is an inextensible geodesic \[LongDash] a shortest path \
that no neighbour of either end prolongs.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"75b48a32-1e3d-4144-98ee-30ad3a0b3188"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Its graph \[LongDash] ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell[
      TextData["InfraMeasurement"]], 
     "paclet:WolframInstitute/SyntheticInfrageometry/ref/InfraMeasurement", 
     "WolframInstitute/SyntheticInfrageometry Package Symbol"},
    "PackageLink",
    BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"], "[", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["g", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["line", "TI"], ",", " ", "\"\<Graph\>\""}], "]"}]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "bd9b51cd-a9bd-4b5c-8787-e25ba2d5bb6c"],
 " \[LongDash] is a ",
 Cell[BoxData["List"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d29ebe9b-5fa9-41ad-8935-df410426dfd8"],
 " of DAGs, one per pair of ends (",
 StyleBox["a", "TI"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["b", "TI"],
 ") that is compatible, ",
 StyleBox["d(a, b) = d(a, p) + d(p, q) + d(q, b)", "TI"],
 ", and maximal, no neighbour of ",
 StyleBox["a", "TI"],
 " or ",
 StyleBox["b", "TI"],
 " lengthening ",
 StyleBox["d(a, b)", "TI"],
 ". The DAG for (",
 StyleBox["a", "TI"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["b", "TI"],
 ") is the union of the intervals ",
 StyleBox["I(a, p)", "TI"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["I(p, q)", "TI"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["I(q, b)", "TI"],
 ". Its chains are exactly the lines with those ends, and every line is a \
chain of exactly one DAG, so ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<Faithful\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "414602a3-ad30-4c75-9c2e-bc6de600c524"],
 " is ",
 Cell[BoxData["True"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f9e7bdbb-b6c4-4502-af4d-9d6464553866"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"4679ae23-9591-4f36-81f4-69dda0457066"],

Cell["\<\
The list is not optional. The union of the DAGs can carry chains that are not \
geodesics: through the edge 1\[Dash]2 of the 6-cycle there are three DAGs and \
three lines, while their union would add a fourth path that is not a geodesic.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"b26277be-ad67-4569-b45c-b941e93c6b24"],

Cell["\<\
The DAGs are alternatives, so the counts add across them. The family can be \
astronomical while the list stays small.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"b79bb170-9c75-43fe-bc9b-c9ac00de4327"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "With ",
 StyleBox["p", "TI"],
 " = ",
 StyleBox["q", "TI"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell[
      TextData["InfraLine"]], 
     "paclet:WolframInstitute/SyntheticInfrageometry/ref/InfraLine", 
     "WolframInstitute/SyntheticInfrageometry Package Symbol"},
    "PackageLink",
    BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"], "[", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["p", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["p", "TI"]}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "492c9e59-0dea-4e5a-a97c-ad17d892ceef"],
 " is every maximal geodesic through ",
 StyleBox["p", "TI"],
 ", once per orientation."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"c261d0ea-4f0e-4c58-b6a5-c30ea1118f0a"]
}, Open  ]],

